drm/asahi: T6040 (M4 Pro) on the macOS 27.2 GPU firmware

nixos-aurora's driver supports the M4 Pro's macOS 26.6.2 GPU firmware
(25G83). This adds the 27.2 build as variant V27_2, which keeps the 25G83
initialization graph with the layout and protocol changes of 27.2. Derived
from a static decode of the 27.2 firmware and macOS 27.2 snapshots
(github:briheet/nixos-m4pro docs/gpu/driver-27.2-diff.md, probe log
driver-27.2-probes.md). Needs aura's three-segment GPU handoff
(../aura-patches/0001).

Identification and segments:
- hw/t6040.rs: the 27.2 loaded image (TEXT 0x64000, DATA 0xc4000, entropy
  0x5d88c/0x5d96f, sha256 eda53a91...).
- data_segment.rs: the firmware asks for its RTKit buffers in its third
  segment, __DATA_SHARED_RO (apple,fw-data-shared-ro).

InitData (fw/initdata/v27_2.rs, initdata/v25g83.rs):
- interface version 0x0c8b6339839804c0; opening record 0x15;
- MainConfig: power_config_va at +0x481, no +0x18 page, +0x308/+0x30c,
  +0x320..+0x328 as macOS;
- hardware data, power configuration, power state and Region C moved to
  their 27.2 offsets in runs, with macOS 27.2's constants (each checked
  word by word against macOS's blocks at its InitData message);
  hardware data +0x2730 stays 0 so the firmware installs the queues;
- status B's recovery and firmware-control words 0x1e0 later; +0xe714 = 1.

Runtime:
- device control: scheduler-state release 0x13 (27.2's 0x14 stores through
  the record), the 27.2 power-assert rule (0x08, 0x09, 0x0a, 0x29), the live
  Region C fields 4 bytes later; the host idle timestamp (Region C +0x98c,
  record 0x22) before keep-powered, as macOS;
- queues: the A18 Pro pointer layout, 0x80-byte (M5) queue records for
  render and compute, a render configuration with every kick, kick-entry
  dependency control bits 63:48 = 0x0fa0.

